record pixelkit.evidence.crate-package-contents/1 : evidence {
    title "cargo package lists and leaf-crate verification for all seven crates"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:900358ac8a7157d11394af01f71fb52e3bda2628
    command "for c in liminalkit-raster liminalkit-text liminalkit-shell liminalkit-ui liminalkit-windowing liminalkit-kms liminalkit; do cargo package --list -p $c --allow-dirty; done && cargo package -p liminalkit-raster --allow-dirty"
    summary """
        Every crate's package list holds only its sources, README, examples and manifest; liminalkit-text also ships the two Noto test fonts and their README (needed by `test-fonts`); liminalkit picks up the workspace README. liminalkit-raster packages to 26 files, 247 KiB (67.7 KiB compressed) and the packaged copy builds. Every manifest carries a description, keywords (at most five, each at most 20 characters) and categories. No publish or dry run was performed.
        """
    author "dk"
}

record pixelkit.evidence.fonts-out-of-package-and-tests/1 : evidence {
    title "Fonts absent from the text crate's package; every test configuration passes at 0.5.0"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:ff2315c93c237e14189144d502e41d550c0b9b1e
    command "cargo package --list -p liminalkit-text --allow-dirty && cargo package -p liminalkit-raster --allow-dirty && cargo test --workspace && cargo test -p liminalkit-text --features bidi && cargo test -p liminalkit -p liminalkit-ui --features liminalkit/accessibility,liminalkit-ui/accessibility && cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --features liminalkit/accessibility,liminalkit/bidi -- -D warnings && cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings && RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --features liminalkit/accessibility,liminalkit/bidi && cargo fmt --all --check && cargo run -p liminalkit-ui --example gallery"
    summary """
        liminalkit-text's package list is Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, README.md, examples/glyph_sheet.rs and src/: no font files. liminalkit-raster packages as 0.5.0 (26 files, 247.6 KiB) and the packaged copy builds. Without any feature the workspace passes 548 tests, 0 failed, including the two tests of the new fixtures crate; 83 pass in liminalkit-text with bidi; 191 with accessibility. Clippy with and without features, rustdoc and fmt are clean. The gallery example renders with no feature flag.
        """
    author "dk"
}

record pixelkit.evidence.frame-bench-resolution-sweep/1 : evidence {
    title "Headless frame cost from 720p to 4K on one laptop"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:b3c1c783af118feaa6d6cad39fd3f34ad01d5384
    command "cargo run --release -p liminalkit --features test-fonts --example frame_bench"
    artifact "crates/liminalkit/examples/frame_bench.rs"
    summary """
        Full redraw of one operational screen (panel, 40-row table, 60-row list, six label sizes, AA shapes), warm text cache, 60 frames, on a 13th Gen Intel i7-13700H laptop: 1280x720 p50 1.03 ms / p95 1.14 ms, 7.9 MiB resident; 1920x1080 p50 1.97 / p95 2.27 ms, 12.6 MiB; 1920x1080 at 1.5x p50 2.07 / p95 2.38 ms; 2560x1440 at 1.5x p50 3.23 / p95 3.76 ms, 27.6 MiB; 3840x2160 at 2x p50 9.77 / p95 11.04 ms, 45.2 MiB. Cold first frames 10 to 42 ms. Cost is close to linear in pixel count; 4K is under one 60 Hz frame for a full repaint. liminalkit only: no egui or Freya comparison yet.
        """
    author "dk"
}

